WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.153
Thirty officers. Twelve posts. Four volunteers. One unfilled post.

00:00:04.153 --> 00:00:08.490
The lieutenant needs to decide who gets the next call.

00:00:09.590 --> 00:00:13.439
ReliefLedger brings the roster, posts, and overtime bucket together.

00:00:13.439 --> 00:00:16.861
This demonstration uses fictional officers and example rules.

00:00:16.861 --> 00:00:20.710
Start with the roster and review the four volunteers.

00:00:21.810 --> 00:00:26.994
Next, select the unfilled post. Check the time and the qualification needed,

00:00:26.994 --> 00:00:30.450
then ask ReliefLedger to evaluate the available officers.

00:00:31.550 --> 00:00:35.966
Review the bucket. The recommendation shows the order and the reason behind

00:00:35.966 --> 00:00:38.910
it, using the rules configured for this demonstration.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:44.810
The lieutenant stays in control. Record the contact outcome, then confirm the

00:00:44.810 --> 00:00:49.610
officer for the unfilled post. ReliefLedger saves the assignment and updates the

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:50.410
overtime bucket.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:53.823
Open the history to review the decision.

00:00:53.823 --> 00:00:57.788
The contact, assignment, and supporting details remain available in a record you

00:00:57.788 --> 00:00:59.110
can review or print.

00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:04.247
ReliefLedger. Built around your facility’s overtime management needs.

00:01:04.247 --> 00:01:06.770
Let’s talk about your facility.
